# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Distant particle event: bremsstrahlung from electrons (exp(-E/200 keV)) precipitating
# over 90000 km2 at 10 deg Earth-central angle (1272 km away, zenith 119.5 deg,
# azimuth 90 deg from north). Peak precipitating flux 4e+04 e/cm2/s above 50 keV.
# Peak photon flux at COSI 0.337 ph/cm2/s; Flux below is the lightcurve-averaged value.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw 73.38 deg. Direction in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R1_DISTPAR0004
R1_DISTPAR0004.ParticleType 1
R1_DISTPAR0004.Beam FarFieldGaussian 117.222 331.458 6.759
R1_DISTPAR0004.Spectrum File R1_DISTPAR0004_spectrum.dat
R1_DISTPAR0004.Flux 0.0932199
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835519625.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): R1_DISTPAR0004_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
R1_DISTPAR0004.Lightcurve File false R1_DISTPAR0004_lightcurve_shifted.dat
R1_DISTPAR0004.EarthOccultation false
